<title>NORWAY: Statoil extends Smedvig deal.</title>
<headline>Statoil extends Smedvig deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Offshore group Smedvig ASA said on Friday state Norwegian oil company Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) had extended a platform drilling contract on the North Sea Statfjord oilfield for a further five years.</p>
<p>The deal was worth between $125-150 million, Smedvig said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The contract covers production drilling, maintenance and support for other types of well operations on all three Statfjord platforms.</p>
<p>Smedvig said it had held the contract on Statfjord since 1987. The new extension will provide work for around 250 people and is scheduled to start as an uninterupted continuation of the current contract period.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
